{"term":"puzzle","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:789e26ea54b64ef0be","definition":"The state of feeling confused or mystified because one cannot understand a complicated matter, a problem, etc.; bewilderment, confusion; (countable) often in in a puzzle: an instance of this.","example":"Certainly, Men in Great Fortunes, are ſtrangers to themſelues, and vvhile they are in the puſle of buſineſſe, they haue no time to tend their Health, either of Body, or Minde.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["bafflement","perplexity"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"uncountable","wordFamily":["befuzzle","bepuzzle","confuzzle","empuzzle","lawyer's puzzle","metapuzzle","monkey puzzle","piece of the puzzle","puzzle box","puzzle canon","puzzle cube","puzzledom","puzzle feeder","puzzlefest","puzzle game","puzzlehead","puzzleheaded","puzzlehunt","puzzle jug","puzzleless","puzzlelike","puzzle lock","puzzlemaster","Puzzle Palace","puzzle-peg","puzzle ring","puzzlery","puzzlesome","puzzlewit","puzzlist"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/puzzle#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ea1b1d0d2763e2a499","definition":"A thing such as a complicated matter or a problem which is difficult to make sense of or understand; also, a person who is difficult to make sense of or understand; an enigma.","example":"Where he went after he left the house is a puzzle.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["anybody's guess","anyone's guess","conundrum","mystery","crux"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable","wordFamily":["befuzzle","bepuzzle","confuzzle","empuzzle","lawyer's puzzle","metapuzzle","monkey puzzle","piece of the puzzle","puzzle box","puzzle canon","puzzle cube","puzzledom","puzzle feeder","puzzlefest","puzzle game","puzzlehead","puzzleheaded","puzzlehunt","puzzle jug","puzzleless","puzzlelike","puzzle lock","puzzlemaster","Puzzle Palace","puzzle-peg","puzzle ring","puzzlery","puzzlesome","puzzlewit","puzzlist"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/puzzle#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:dd7a16a9c763ae9992","definition":"Often preceded by a descriptive word: a game or toy, or a problem, requiring some effort to complete or work out, which is intended as a pastime and/or to test one's mental ability.","example":"crossword puzzle    jigsaw puzzle","pos":"noun","synonyms":["brainteaser","poser"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable","wordFamily":["befuzzle","bepuzzle","confuzzle","empuzzle","lawyer's puzzle","metapuzzle","monkey puzzle","piece of the puzzle","puzzle box","puzzle canon","puzzle cube","puzzledom","puzzle feeder","puzzlefest","puzzle game","puzzlehead","puzzleheaded","puzzlehunt","puzzle jug","puzzleless","puzzlelike","puzzle lock","puzzlemaster","Puzzle Palace","puzzle-peg","puzzle ring","puzzlery","puzzlesome","puzzlewit","puzzlist"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/puzzle#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:4d108adfc57bef292f","definition":"Short for puzzle-peg (“a piece of wood secured under a dog's jaw to keep the dog's nose away from the ground so that it uses the scent in the air to track its quarry, and to prevent the dog from tearing the quarry once found”).","example":"So I ſent for a carpenter, on the receipt of your recipe, and had a large Puzzle of Oak made for him [a dog], after the pattern of thoſe vvorn by the Squire's Pointers; and I have found it anſvver prodigiouſly.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"abbreviation, alt-of, obsolete","register":"abbreviation, alt-of, countable, obsolete","wordFamily":["befuzzle","bepuzzle","confuzzle","empuzzle","lawyer's puzzle","metapuzzle","monkey puzzle","piece of the puzzle","puzzle box","puzzle canon","puzzle cube","puzzledom","puzzle feeder","puzzlefest","puzzle game","puzzlehead","puzzleheaded","puzzlehunt","puzzle jug","puzzleless","puzzlelike","puzzle lock","puzzlemaster","Puzzle Palace","puzzle-peg","puzzle ring","puzzlery","puzzlesome","puzzlewit","puzzlist"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/puzzle#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:7c58f3b7ce31d12b8f","definition":"To cause (oneself or someone, or their mind, etc.) to feel confused or mystified because they cannot understand a complicated matter, a problem, etc.; to confuse, to mystify, to perplex.","example":"Mens daily occaſions for themſelves or friends, and the neceſities of common life, require the doing of a thouſand things vvithin the compaſs of a fevv dayes, for vvhich it vvould puzzle the beſt Textman that liveth; readily to bethink himself of a ſentence in the Bible, clear enough to ſatisfie a ſcrupulous conſcience of the lavvfulneſs and expediency of vvhat he is about to do; […]","pos":"verb","synonyms":["empuzzle","addle","baffle","vex","lose","embroil","stick","stump","baffound","bamboozle","bedevil","befuddle","throw","bemud","bemuse","bewilder","bumfuzzle","complicate","confound","confuddle","confuse","confuzzle","dazzle","discombobulate","disconcert","blind","dumbfound","entangle","ferhoodle","flabagast","flabbergast","flabbergaster","flurry","fluster","flummox","fuddle","jumble","knot","mix up","muddle","muddy","ravel","perplex","puzzle"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"also, reflexive","register":"also, reflexive, transitive","wordFamily":["befuzzle","bepuzzle","confuzzle","empuzzle","lawyer's puzzle","metapuzzle","monkey puzzle","piece of the puzzle","puzzle box","puzzle canon","puzzle cube","puzzledom","puzzle feeder","puzzlefest","puzzle game","puzzlehead","puzzleheaded","puzzlehunt","puzzle jug","puzzleless","puzzlelike","puzzle lock","puzzlemaster","Puzzle Palace","puzzle-peg","puzzle ring","puzzlery","puzzlesome","puzzlewit","puzzlist"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/puzzle#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b8a7a1db400e0e4648","definition":"To use (one's brain or mind) to try to work out a complicated matter, a problem, etc.; also, to try to work out (a complicated matter, a problem, etc.).","example":"VVhich puſles the braine, and doth confound the ſence, / VVhich makes vs rather beare thoſe euilles vve haue, / Than flie to others that vve knovv knot of.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["befuzzle","bepuzzle","confuzzle","empuzzle","lawyer's puzzle","metapuzzle","monkey puzzle","piece of the puzzle","puzzle box","puzzle canon","puzzle cube","puzzledom","puzzle feeder","puzzlefest","puzzle game","puzzlehead","puzzleheaded","puzzlehunt","puzzle jug","puzzleless","puzzlelike","puzzle lock","puzzlemaster","Puzzle Palace","puzzle-peg","puzzle ring","puzzlery","puzzlesome","puzzlewit","puzzlist"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/puzzle#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0fd2efe5ec63aec812","definition":"To (intentionally) make (something) complicated or confused, and so difficult to resolve or understand; to confuse, to complicate.","example":"[T]hey are theſe Talkative Fools, vvhoſe Religion is only in vvord, and are debauched and vain in their Converſation, that (being ſo much admitted into the fellovv-ſhip of the godly) do puzzle the VVorld, blemiſh Chriſtianity, and grieve the ſincere.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["confound","entangle","muddle","obfuscate"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete, transitive","wordFamily":["befuzzle","bepuzzle","conf